  { q: "Why is the Butterfly Lovers called China's Romeo and Juliet?", a: "It earns this nickname because both stories feature young, star-crossed lovers whose romance is forbidden by their families and ends in a double tragedy. However, the Chinese legend adds unique cultural elements like cross-dressing for education and a magical transformation into butterflies." },
